{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/workflow-server/pulls/893","id":4592848751,"node_id":"PR_kwDOQ8oa8s8AAAABEcFPbw","html_url":"https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/pull/893","diff_url":"https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/pull/893.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/pull/893.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/workflow-server/issues/893","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/workflow-server/pulls/893/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/workflow-server/pulls/893/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/workflow-server/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/workflow-server/issues/893/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/workflow-server/statuses/8243328f88d61105bc6a23de9bcaa8ddce5fe020","number":893,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"[I08:E02] GitNexus library: measure a concern across a repository group","user":{"login":"m2ux","id":176900785,"node_id":"U_kgDOCotKsQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176900785?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux","html_url":"https://github.com/m2ux","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n\nThe gitnexus library gains a run that measures how far a concern in one member of a repository group reaches into every other member, with three operations the run composes and a specimen that walks it against a real group of a library and its consumers. Closes #881.\n\n## What happens today\n\nEvery impact and context answer is addressed at one named graph, and a graph holds nodes only for the symbols its own tree defines. A name a tree imports from a package built elsewhere has no node, and import edges run file to file inside the one tree, so a consumer's use of a library's symbol is an edge in no graph: the library's graph never sees the consumer, and the consumer's graph has nothing to hang the edge on. Repository groups offer a merged concept search and a contract registry, and the registry carries a library coupling only where a manifest link in the group's configuration declares it; the automatic shared-library detection the configuration names is not wired in this GitNexus version. A concern's cross-repository reach therefore has no named operation, and the instruments that can answer it are scattered.\n\n## The change\n\nThe group-radius run refers to the existing group-refresh run first, so every member graph and the contract registry are current before any claim, and it takes the registry's contract report from that run. It then reads the concern's connections and blast radius in its home graph, taking the identity that reaches one symbol where a name reaches several, maps the routes and tools the home tree serves, and names the boundary another member could reach the concern by: the concern itself, the depth-one dependents that sit in exported files, any route or tool served from those files, and the packages the home is consumed under, read from the manifests above the concern's file and from the registry's library contracts. The concern's own members are left out of the boundary, because their bare names are ones every tree defines. One merged search across the group follows. A loop over the members holds a loop over the boundary names, probing every other member's graph for what depends on each name and recording the answer.\n\nA closing judgement settles each member's reach from three instruments and names each in the answer: the registry's cross-links from the member to the home, the member's own edges with the defining file recorded so a mirror of the home's symbol can be told from a homonym, and a search of the member's tree for the boundary names and the package names. Reach is the first that holds — linked, graph, hand-derived, none — with unanswerable reserved for a member with no graph and no tree, and a member the search reached under a package name with no link declared is named as a coupling the group's configuration is missing. Every entry names the graph it answers for.\n\nThree operations carry the parts a routine cannot hold: listing a group's members as a walkable list with each one's tree and home mark, extracting the boundary, and settling the reach. The namespace's rule on the edges the parser cannot see now names the imported-name case beside macro bodies and type-level references. The gitnexus-radius-conformance specimen refers to the run and writes one row per member with its graph and every instrument asked.\n\n## What was verified\n\n- The full corpus guard sweep over this branch passes, 49 guards, under engine `main`. The loader splices the run with the nested readiness reference composed under the site's prefix, and delivers the home reads with the concern's identity bound at both.\n- On the experiment sidecar serving this branch, the minimum viable workflow walked first, then the specimen walked to completion over a six-member group: a Rust and wasm library as home and five consumers in two languages, one of them carrying no graph. The readiness reference found every graph current and rebuilt none; the registry held four declared library links. The concern's identity resolved one symbol in both home reads, where the name alone reaches four in that tree. No consumer's graph held a node for the imported name: four members settled as linked from the registry, including the one with no graph, and the fifth, which declares no link, settled as hand-derived from thirty-eight files naming the symbol against a package name found only in release notes, recorded as a coupling the links do not declare. The home tree's route inventory failed on that graph and is recorded as unmeasured. Every row names its graph and its instruments. The walk's report is the specimen's declared artifact.\n- Two earlier walks of the same group drove the design here. The first handed the probes the concern's own methods, and a consumer's graph answered one of them with fifty-three dependents of a homonym; that is what the boundary exclusion answers. The second measured a radius by name and received candidates in place of a measurement, having no identity to pass; that is what the identity input answers.\n\n## Non-goals\n\nNo GitNexus engine changes; no new graph schema; single-graph operations unchanged. Automatic detection of package coupling stays with GitNexus.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-09-21T14:51:35Z","updated_at":"2026-10-01T12:45:55Z","closed_at":"2026-09-22T16:35:06Z","merged_at":"2026-09-22T16:35:06Z","merge_commit_sha":"2d8a06d83702132b2042aee315d31a394452ce4f","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"m2ux:workflow/881-gitnexus-group-radius","ref":"workflow/881-gitnexus-group-radius","repo":{"id":1137318642,"node_id":"R_kgDOQ8oa8g","name":"workflow-server","full_name":"m2ux/workflow-server","owner":{"login":"m2ux","id":176900785,"node_id":"U_kgDOCotKsQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176900785?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux","html_url":"https://github.com/m2ux","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/followers","following_url